# Agent-governing instructions are encrypted at rest (git-crypt) to prevent
# third-party contamination / prompt-injection of the files that steer agent
# behavior. Holders of the git-crypt key see plaintext in the working tree;
# everyone else (GitHub, forks, PR authors) sees ciphertext they cannot read
# or meaningfully alter. See agents/ and the root pointer files.
agents/** filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
